cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its results, please cite it as below."
title: "QAPINN-Spectra: Spectrum-Matched Circuit Design for Quantum-Assisted Physics-Informed Neural Networks"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Katta
    given-names: Lahari
  - family-names: Mannava
    given-names: Daasaradhi
version: 1.1.0
date-released: 2026-09-25
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/Mannava-Daasaradhi/QAPINN_Spectra"
abstract: >-
  Spectrum-Matched Circuit Design (SMCD) reads a PDE's target spectral support from its
  operator symbol and constructs a data-re-uploading quantum circuit whose frequency set
  covers it, with no architecture search. Six explainable-AI instruments, run identically
  on matched classical and hybrid physics-informed neural networks, test twelve
  pre-registered predictions about where the quantum layer helps. Finalist, WISER Summer
  Program 2026 Industry Challenge (BQP Challenge).
keywords:
  - physics-informed neural networks
  - quantum machine learning
  - variational quantum circuits
  - spectral bias
  - explainable AI
